# IPA Bundle Analyzer

A production-grade macOS application for analyzing and comparing iOS .ipa files. Built with SwiftUI and modern Swift concurrency.

![macOS](https://img.shields.io/badge/macOS-14.0+-blue)
![Swift](https://img.shields.io/badge/Swift-5.9+-orange)
![SwiftUI](https://img.shields.io/badge/SwiftUI-Latest-green)

## Features

### 🔍 Single IPA Analysis
- **Complete Metadata Extraction**: App name, bundle ID, version, build number, minimum iOS version, device families
- **Size Breakdown**: Binary, frameworks, assets, plugins with hierarchical analysis
- **File Tree Explorer**: Browse complete IPA structure with search and sort capabilities
- **Binary Analysis**: Mach-O parsing for architectures, segments, bitcode detection, and symbol count
- **Framework Analysis**: List embedded frameworks with sizes, versions, and duplicate detection
- **Assets Analysis**: Identify large assets with type categorization and optimization suggestions
- **Interactive Visualizations**: Pie charts, bar charts using Swift Charts

### ⚖️ IPA Comparison
- **Side-by-Side Comparison**: Compare two IPA versions with detailed diff analysis
- **Size Changes**: Track size differences across all categories (binary, frameworks, assets)
- **File-Level Changes**: Added, removed, and modified files with size impact
- **Framework Changes**: Version updates, additions, and removals
- **Binary Changes**: Architecture differences, segment size changes
- **Visual Diff**: Color-coded changes (green=added, red=removed, yellow=modified)
- **Smart Filtering**: View all changes, only significant changes, or large changes (>1MB)

### 📊 Export Options
- **JSON Reports**: Complete analysis in structured JSON format
- **CSV Summaries**: Spreadsheet-friendly data export
- **Comparison Reports**: Detailed diff reports for CI/CD integration

## Technical Stack

- **Language**: Swift 5.9+
- **UI Framework**: SwiftUI with MVVM architecture
- **Concurrency**: async/await for non-blocking operations
- **Charts**: Swift Charts for data visualization
- **File Handling**: Native FileManager with ZIP extraction
- **Binary Parsing**: Custom Mach-O parser

## Architecture

```
IPAAnalyzer/
├── Models/
│   ├── IPAInfo.swift              # Core IPA data model
│   ├── FileNode.swift             # Hierarchical file tree
│   └── ComparisonResult.swift     # Comparison data structures
├── Services/
│   ├── IPAExtractor.swift         # ZIP extraction and validation
│   ├── IPAAnalyzer.swift          # Main analysis orchestrator
│   ├── BinaryParser.swift         # Mach-O binary parsing
│   └── DiffEngine.swift           # IPA comparison engine
├── ViewModels/
│   ├── IPAViewModel.swift         # Single IPA analysis state
│   └── ComparisonViewModel.swift  # Comparison state management
└── Views/
    ├── DashboardView.swift        # Main analysis interface
    ├── FileTreeView.swift         # File explorer
    ├── ChartsView.swift           # Data visualizations
    ├── BinaryView.swift           # Binary details
    ├── FrameworksView.swift       # Framework listing
    ├── AssetsView.swift           # Assets analysis
    └── Comparison/
        ├── ComparisonView.swift   # Comparison interface
        └── ... (comparison detail views)
```

## Usage

### Single IPA Analysis

1. **Open an IPA**:
   - Use File → Open IPA (⌘O)
   - Drag and drop an .ipa file onto the window
   
2. **Explore Analysis**:
   - **Overview**: View metadata and size summary
   - **Files**: Browse file tree with search
   - **Binary**: Examine Mach-O details
   - **Frameworks**: List embedded frameworks
   - **Assets**: View large assets
   - **Charts**: Interactive visualizations

3. **Export Results**:
   - Export JSON for programmatic access
   - Export CSV for spreadsheet analysis

### IPA Comparison

1. **Load Two IPAs**:
   - Click "Compare" tab
   - Select first IPA (newer version)
   - Select second IPA (older version)
   
2. **Review Changes**:
   - **Overview**: High-level comparison summary
   - **Size Changes**: Detailed size impact analysis
   - **File Changes**: Added/removed/modified files
   - **Framework Changes**: Framework updates
   - **Binary Changes**: Architecture and segment diffs

3. **Filter Results**:
   - All changes
   - Only changes (hide unchanged)
   - Large changes only (>1MB)

4. **Export Comparison**:
   - JSON comparison report
   - CSV diff summary

## Requirements

- macOS 14.0 or later
- Xcode 15.0 or later (for building)

## Building

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone <repository-url>
cd IPAAnalyzer

# Open in Xcode
open IPAAnalyzer.xcodeproj

# Build and run (⌘R)
```

## Performance

- Handles large IPAs (>500MB)
- Background processing for extraction and analysis
- Lazy loading for file trees
- Non-blocking UI with progress indicators

## Features in Detail

### Binary Analysis
- **Architecture Detection**: arm64, armv7, x86_64
- **Segment Analysis**: __TEXT, __DATA, __LINKEDIT sizes
- **Bitcode Detection**: Check for bitcode presence
- **Symbol Count**: Total symbol count (when available)

### Framework Analysis
- **Size Tracking**: Per-framework size breakdown
- **Version Detection**: Extract framework versions from Info.plist
- **Duplicate Detection**: Identify duplicate frameworks
- **Sorting**: By name or size

### Assets Analysis
- **Type Categorization**: Images, videos, audio, fonts, assets catalogs
- **Size Threshold**: Only show assets >100KB
- **Search & Filter**: Find specific assets by name or type
- **Optimization Hints**: Identify large assets for optimization

### Comparison Features
- **Smart Diffing**: Efficient file-level comparison
- **Size Impact**: Show size increase/decrease with percentages
- **Version Tracking**: Compare app versions and build numbers
- **Framework Versions**: Track framework version changes

## Error Handling

- Invalid IPA validation
- Corrupted ZIP detection
- Missing Payload folder handling
- Binary parsing failures with fallback to `otool`
- User-friendly error messages

## Future Enhancements

- [ ] Unused asset detection
- [ ] Duplicate file identification
- [ ] Size optimization recommendations
- [ ] CLI support for CI/CD integration
- [ ] HTML report generation
- [ ] App Store size estimation

